  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "D.Rajkumar vs / on 8 November, 2024 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.(MD)No.46 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 08.11.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.(MD)No.4624 of 2018 and W.M.P.(MD)No.4704 & 4705 of 2018 D.Rajkumar ... And Chief Wildlife Warden, Panagal Maaligai, Saidapet, Chennai 600 015. 2.The Wildlife Warden, O/o. The Wildlife Warden, No.110, Public Office Road, Nagapattinam. ... Respond Prayer: Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of Ind issue a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamus to call for the records per to the impugned order in Se.Mu.Aanai.No.VaVu1/26500/2016 dated 19.12.2016 passed by the 1st respondent and quash the same and consequently directing the respondents to issue necessary transport permission to the elephant as per rules and considering the schedul the temple festival during auspicious days. 1/6 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.P.(M For Petitioner : Mr.R.Narayanan For Respondents : Mr.M.Senthil Ayyanar Special Government Pleader D.Rajkumar vs / on 8 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/117437578/ 1 Order",
    "facts": "They used to transport their https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis elephants without giving enough rest to the elephants between functions and also without following the Tamil Nadu Captive Elephants (Management and Maintenance) Rules, 2011. Therefore, in order to avoid cruel act meted out to the captive elephants by the elephant owners in maintaining and treating the elephants and to regulate the method of transporting captive elephants and their work in functions in proper way, certain guidelines have been framed under the aforesaid Rules.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
